From 2da7b4ba880243a0742ad353f96b3d3f2950f5f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:25:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! chain: give Lotus V2 its own data directory, ports and
 network identity

Handle new networks with no trusted checkpoints: the seeder advertises required height0 and snapshots an optional checkpoint per peer instead of dereferencing an empty map. Keep checkpoint verification unchanged for networks that supply one.

Use a test-local synthetic checkpoint to preserve locator, accepted-header and wrong-chain rejection coverage without altering immutable global chain parameters. Add a real empty-mainnet-checkpoint case checking no GETHEADERS requirement and acceptance of unsolicited headers. Native focused p2p_messaging_tests passes all9cases; before leaf failed and later cases dereferenced the empty map.

Tier: V2
